b-workbench .wb-cmd-line[hidden],\n.nb-workbench .wb-conflict[hidden],\n.nb-workbench .wm-form[hidden],","old":".nb-workbench .wb-conflict[hidden],\n.nb-workbench .wm-form[hidden],","patch_id":"p130","time":1793223163745},{"author":"promote","cmd":"","facet":"memory","label":"promote: fold -> dev.workbench","new":"[\n{\"claim\": \"The workbench's command rows resolve language and signature from TWO reads: the command record (readRec of cmdEntry.id) carries only {name, type, <lang>: implId} — params, returntype, desc, tags and groups all live on the impl record, so row rendering and the details/meta panels fetch cmdRec then impl. The row's open action must use the type resolved at click time, never the commandLang() guess from the entry's legacy language keys (java ids linger on rust commands).\", \"detail\": \"Established during the 2026-10-29 commands redesign (branch workbench-commands-redesign, commit 202584d7). The old addCodeOpen captured the guessed lang in a closure, so the code pane could open with a stale badge; the redesign keeps one mutable state.lang per row that the async resolve updates and the click handler reads.\", \"tags\": \"dev.workbench,command-records,impl-records,resolved-type\", \"confidence\": \"high\", \"time\": 1793224945269},\n{\"claim\": \"The workbench's delete-command Revert re-authors from the journal entry: delete_command's `old` is {command, impl} record data with attachments INLINED (store.get_data reads attachment keys back), so upsert_command(lang, returntype, params, import, body from impl[ext]) — write_flow_body for flows — restores the command; desc/tags/groups are then re-applied from the same `old` because upsert_command carries neither and does not journal, so the restore leaves no second journal entry.\", \"detail\": \"Shipped in commit 202584d7 (branch workbench-commands-redesign). The body key is rs for rust, the lang name otherwise (python/flow). The delete toast is the workbench's OWN persistent .wb-toast with a Revert